From b99ddb81566d022cbbf45617a51483a35737fb1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:30:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dashboard-auth): let core session-header service calls
 pass the gated dashboard [daveey]

hermes plugins enable/install posts /api/dashboard/agent-plugins/activate, and the
review-retire path reads /api/health/idle and posts /api/health/retirement, with
X-Hermes-Session-Token and no cookie. On a gated dashboard (auth_required) the cookie
gate refused them as no_cookie before the handler ran (104x on the MacBook, 51x on
the mini since 10-12), so plugin activation never reached open Desktop chats while
the CLI printed only the gateway's success.

- token seam: register_token_route(path, session_token_check=...) registers an exact
  path that accepts the deployment session token (same constant-time check as
  _require_token) on a gated app; without a valid token the request passes to the
  cookie/native gates unchanged. web_server registers exactly the three service paths
  (SESSION_TOKEN_SERVICE_ROUTES); _require_token accepts that principal when gated.
- notify_serve_backend logs a refused/unreachable backend at warning with status and
  reason (never the token) and activation_hint names it: 'The Desktop backend did not
  load it (401 Unauthorized); open Desktop chats get it after that backend restarts.'
  A backend that loaded it is shown too; no backend record says nothing new.
- recurrence test: every hermes_cli/gateway caller sending the session header must
  target a registered session-token route.
